        "title": "Interesting but not that exciting ",
        "text": "Pashupatinath definitely gives you a nice insight into Hindu culture, but it is one of the least exciting things I got to do in Kathmandu. You are not allowed into the main part as its so sacred only Hindus (and Buddhists as I found out) are allowed entry. It is interesting to see the surrounding, especially the ghats by the river where cremations regularly take place. I would try to go, but dont be sad if you miss it. If you do go, be sure to include the amazing Boudhanath Stupa into that day, as its very close (I walked). For that, you have to walk up the hill across from Pashupatinath. There you can also see a beautiful maze of little temples in a small forrest.",
