        "title": "Mystical, Spiritual - a place where pilgrams go some to die",
        "text": "The Pashupatinath Temple is located on both banks of Bagmati River on the eastern outskirts of Kathmandu. Its one of the most pillars of scared spaces for Hindu worshippers dedicated to Lord Shiva.\nThe architecture of the temple is worth a visit ad if you visited the Ganges River in India this temple site is similar.\nWe visited in December when the Indian currency was changed making it difficult for Indians to access their money. While the Temple still attracted thousand of worshippers Nepalese told us there were far less pilgrims then other years Only believers of Shiva are allowed into the temple. There also is a entrance fee which is much steeper for tourists. The dead are burnt and the ashes committed to the river. The sacred space is a pace where many people around the world (older, the sick) etc come to die.\nIf sacred spaces is for you don't miss Pashupati this sacred Hindi temple is also mystical in a spiritual way.",
